      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear the overwhelming fear in your words that nothing is real or stable, and it is honest to feel that searching for empty. When looking outward finds nothing, it often helps to simply stay connected with the immediate sensation of breathing and the stability of your own thoughts. Trusting that small, internal experience can become a new kind of grounding without requiring grand structures or explanations. You do not need a reason for being right now, other than the very presence of your consciousness to ask these questions.",
      "source": "target",
